{
  "brand": "samsung",
  "contractVersion": "1.1",
  "notes": [
    "Only sources that have returned a real price in a live run are enabled=true.",
    "parser=jsonld-itemlist reads a schema.org ItemList (brand listing page or retailer category page) and emits one record per model+variant, keeping the lowest listed price. This is what keeps the model list in sync with each market.",
    "parser=jsonld reads a single product page's schema.org Product/Offer. The model/variant are derived from the page title and must agree with the configured model, otherwise the source fails instead of mislabelling a price.",
    "parser=extra-search discovers the current product URL through eXtra's public Unbxd search API (apiKey/siteKey are read from the storefront search page) and then confirms the price on the product page's own JSON-LD. Used for the OMR-denominated Oman market, whose search page is JS/Unbxd-driven but whose product pages expose static JSON-LD.",
    "Model identity keeps connectivity and S-series sub-model (A17 vs A17 5G, S26 vs S26+ vs S26 Ultra vs S26 FE); collapsing them previously let a different phone's lowest price win the cell. Bundle/combo listings are rejected because their price includes accessories.",
    "parser=amazon-search renders the local Amazon storefront with Playwright, matches model + storage in a result card, verifies the product page when reachable, otherwise uses the card price (amazon-search-card).",
    "parser=browser-text renders a product page with Playwright and extracts a localized price token.",
    "Countries without a reachable source (om) keep enabled=false and a reason; they show as unavailable instead of a guessed price.",
    "A pinned `asin` lets the Amazon parser go straight to /dp/<asin> (a much smaller request than the search grid) which is the reliable path from datacenter IPs; it was captured from a real product page, not invented.",
    "`modelOverride` pins a source to an explicit, human-verified model id when the retailer's title format hides the connectivity suffix (e.g. Jumbo: \"Galaxy A27 8GB RAM 5G Smartphone\" -> \"A27 5G\"). It is the only path that is allowed to skip the page-vs-config model equality guard, and it exists so such a source lands on the SAME model row instead of splitting the matrix and the trend series.",
    "Jumbo Electronics (jumbo.ae) publishes static schema.org Product JSON-LD and is readable from datacenter IPs, so the UAE retail channel does not depend on Amazon, which refuses GitHub runner IPs."
  ],
